// Each prefix states one independently accepted condition from issue #300. The reproduction
// workflow requires these checks to fail on the frozen PR #484 implementation. The complete
// current-output check first proves that every named struct and control case is present, so a
// missing label or truncated output cannot masquerade as a reproduced gap.

// EQUIVALENT-LABEL: struct.def @EquivalentConditionGap
// EQUIVALENT: } {product_source = "fused"}
// EQUIVALENT-LABEL: struct.def @ResultfulConstrainGap

// RESULTFUL-LABEL: struct.def @ResultfulConstrainGap
// RESULTFUL: } {product_source = "fused"}
// RESULTFUL-LABEL: struct.def @CombinedGap

// COMBINED-LABEL: struct.def @CombinedGap
// COMBINED: } {product_source = "fused"}
// COMBINED-LABEL: struct.def @DifferentPredicateControl
